    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-053. Marks the ADR as Implemented with a **test-verified delta**.\n\n## The verified delta\n\n**644 → 647 test cases, 2465 → 2471 assertions. All pass.**\n\n- **1 test flipped in place**: the ADR-037-era `\"max-width: containing vw is skipped (not collapsed)\"` test became `\"max-width: containing vw now clamps (ADR-053)\"`, expecting `100` (was `400`). That's the clamp firing on `min(100px, 75vw)` @ vw=800.\n- **3 new tests**: `max-width: 100vw` → 800, `max-height: 100vh` → 600, `max-height: calc(100vh - 48px)` → 552.\n\nEach new test uses explicit 5000px natural size so the clamp actually activates (natural size must exceed max for the `max < natural` condition to hold).\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero visible PNG delta.** `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` is `h=0` from ancestor culling. The clamp fires but the element has nothing to clamp. Same category as ADR-047/048: correct infrastructure before consumer.\n\n**What changes semantically**: three viewport-unit max clamps now compute correct pixel values. Any future un-culling immediately gets a correctly-clamped box.\n\n## Honest correction to spec\n\nADR-053 spec claimed \"no existing test relies on unclamped behavior.\" **That claim was wrong.** One test did — `\"max-width: containing vw is skipped (not collapsed)\"` — and it was the exact test that needed to flip. Updated in place with an explanatory comment, per the pattern ADR-051 used when `parse_operand` discovery forced a test change.\n\n## What this PR carries\n\n- ADR-053 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-053 note in ADR-051 (viewport units now honored by clamps, remaining prerequisites enumerated)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Prerequisite chain\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `@supports (display: grid)` gate | ✅ ADR-050 |\n| `calc(100vh - 48px)` parses | ✅ ADR-051 |\n| `viewport_h` in production | ✅ ADR-052 |\n| Layout reads `max-height` | ✅ ADR-053 |\n| Ancestor culling | ❌ pending (separate) |\n| `position: sticky` scroll-Y | ❌ pending (separate) |\n\n## Test count\n\n- 647 cases / 2471 assertions all pass\n- Documentation only; no code changes\n\nRefs #240\n",
